{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh rose.</b> From his bed." "<b>Night.</b> And not in the manner of kings — at three hours into the day (ibid.)." "<b>He.</b> First, and afterward <b>his servants</b> — this teaches that he himself went around to the houses of his servants and stood them up (ibid.)." "<b>For there was no house where there was not one dead.</b> If there was a firstborn there — he died; if there was no firstborn — the eldest of the house is called 'firstborn,' as it is said: ״אַף אֲנִי בְּכוֹר אֶתְנֶנְהוּ״ (Psalms 89). Another matter: the Egyptian women would commit adultery under their husbands and bear children from unmarried bachelors, and they had many firstborns — sometimes five to one woman, each one a firstborn to his father."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:46.326075219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}